OL,3,GNEWSAAirliner narrowly misses gliders
OL,4,Aon approach to Luton
OL,5,
OL,6,FAir traffic controllers were left
OL,7,Fshaken after the pilot of an
OL,8,Fapproaching airliner said they had
OL,9,Fnarrowly missed four gliders - one of
OL,10,Fwhich was clocked flying at 5,000ft.
OL,12,FThe incident happened on 27 April close
OL,13,Fto Leighton Buzzard, Bedfordshire, as
OL,14,Fthe Airbus A321 came in to land at
OL,15,FLuton Airport.
OL,17,FAccording to a report by UK Airprox
OL,18,FBoard the "gliders appeared to be
OL,19,Foperating in, or very close to,
OL,20,Fcontrolled airspace at the same level
OL,21,Fas their aircraft".
OL,23,APub: 17-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB E Eng NewsC  Reg TVF Weather
